# org-fixture graph, N-Triples subset. Planted hazards are labelled in
# fixtures/README.md; the correct stamp for every triple below is known
# in advance and asserted by the test suite.
#
# --- typing triples ---
<ex:Alice> <rdf:type> <ex:Employee> .
<ex:Bob> <rdf:type> <ex:Person> .
<ex:Carol> <rdf:type> <ex:Employee> .
<ex:Dave> <rdf:type> <ex:Person> .
<ex:Erin> <rdf:type> <ex:Person> .
<ex:Acme> <rdf:type> <ex:Organization> .
<ex:Jacksonville> <rdf:type> <ex:City> .
# Pat is typed into two disjoint classes -> DISJOINT_CLASS (both lines).
<ex:Pat> <rdf:type> <ex:Person> .
<ex:Pat> <rdf:type> <ex:Organization> .
# Wizard is not a declared class -> UNKNOWN_CLASS.
<ex:Zed> <rdf:type> <ex:Wizard> .
#
# --- conformant triples ---
<ex:Alice> <ex:worksFor> <ex:Acme> .
<ex:Acme> <ex:locatedIn> <ex:Jacksonville> .
<ex:Bob> <ex:mentors> <ex:Alice> .
<ex:Carol> <ex:hasManager> <ex:Dave> .
#
# --- planted violations ---
# Second distinct manager for Carol; hasManager allows at most 1.
<ex:Carol> <ex:hasManager> <ex:Erin> .
# An Organization cannot worksFor anything: domain is Person.
<ex:Acme> <ex:worksFor> <ex:Alice> .
# A City is not an Organization: range of worksFor violated.
<ex:Bob> <ex:worksFor> <ex:Jacksonville> .
# likes is not declared in the ontology.
<ex:Alice> <ex:likes> <ex:Bob> .
#
# --- unverifiable triples (missing evidence, not contradictions) ---
# Ghost has no type triple at all.
<ex:Ghost> <ex:mentors> <ex:Alice> .
# Zed's only type is the undeclared class Wizard.
<ex:Zed> <ex:mentors> <ex:Alice> .
# Rex and Bone are untyped; these two hops also form the planted
# non-composable path (range of owns is Vehicle, domain of eats is
# Animal, and no class sits under both).
<ex:Alice> <ex:owns> <ex:Rex> .
<ex:Rex> <ex:eats> <ex:Bone> .
